[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:62. After the Fire]
[00:00.420]Passage 62 | 文章六十二
[00:02.600]After the fire. | 大火之后。
[00:05.810]Firemen had been fighting the forest fire for nearly three weeks | 消防队员们同那场森林大火搏斗了将近3个星期，
[00:12.105]before they could get it under control. | 才把火势控制住。
[00:15.490]A short time before, great trees had covered the countryside for miles around.| 不久前，参天大树覆盖着方圆数英里的乡村。
[00:23.260]Now, smoke still rose up from the warm ground over the desolate hills.| 而现在，烟依然从温暖的地面上升起，笼罩着荒凉的山丘。
[00:30.775]Winter was coming on, | 冬天即将来临，
[00:33.425]and the hills threatened the surrounding villages with destruction. | 山丘也威胁着将要摧毁周围的村庄。
[00:38.475]For heavy rain would not only wash away the soil, | 因为大雨不仅会冲走泥土，
[00:42.550]but would cause serious floods as well. | 而且会造成严重的水灾。
[00:46.805]When the fire had at last been put out, | 大火终于扑灭之后，
[00:50.925]the forest authorities ordered several tons of a special type of grass seed which would grow quickly. | 森林管理机构订购了好几吨能够快速生长的特殊草籽。
[00:59.490]The seed was sprayed over the ground in huge quantities by airplanes.| 草籽被飞机大量喷洒到地面上。
[01:07.180]The planes had been planting seed for nearly a month when it began to rain.| 飞机撒播草籽将近1个月，天就开始下雨了。
[01:14.360]By then, however, in many places the grass had already taken root.| 然而，到那时，许多地方的草皮已经扎下了根。
[01:21.010]In place of the great trees which had been growing there for centuries,| 昔日参天大树生长了几个世纪的地方，
[01:27.030]patches of green had begun to appear in the blackened soil.| 如今已是一片片绿色在焦黑的土壤上开始显现。